<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Tiwheel yr shr, div surges.</title>
<headline>Tiwheel yr shr, div surges.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     52.0	  vs 36.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 21.0	  vs 14.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   21.66	 vs 14.51</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   27.39	 vs 18.32</p>
<p>    Tax			 6.59	  vs 4.33</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   3.15	  vs 2.70</p>
<p>    Turnover		  360.59	vs 238.58</p>
<p>Full name: Tiger Wheels Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  0.86	  vs 0.52</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors have resolved to award capitalisation shares to shareholders registered on September 27.</p>
<p>They said the prospect of another year of sustained growth was tempered by the possibility of more competitive markets both locally and abroad as well as consumer pressure for price containment.</p>
<p>Tiger Wheels Holdings Ltd, which holds a 64.2 percent stake in Tiwheel, reported earnings per share of 41.5 cents in the year to end June compared to 28.7 cents a year ago.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
